book_lore.book_flower.page.0=remember 当我 mentioned 中 my 第一 memo 该化合物是 mostly anorganic? well guess 什么, 旧 man shared fourth ingredient：ipomoea nil, genus 的 flower. morning glory! 它 might 为由于其低硫 content, 无所谓 might 为 case,
book_lore.book_flower.page.1=它不会 work 带 other flowers. morning glory goes 进入槽位 %d

book_lore.book_syringe.name=便笺
book_lore.book_syringe.author=Dave
book_lore.book_syringe.page.0=little addendum 至 my fifth message, obviously 你 have 至 store 此 MKU stuff 中 container. R&D nuts 使用 regular 金属 syringes 该它们 got 来自 medical. surplus ware 我 presume, 它们 got thousands 的 needles just lying around. 金属
book_lore.book_syringe.page.1=syringe goes 进入槽位 %d

book_lore.resignation_note.name=Letter 的 Resignation
book_lore.resignation_note.author=Kosma
book_lore.resignation_note.page.0=Management downsized 我们的 department 再次 yesterday. 那些 idiots 仅 have themselves 至 blame, 我不要 know 什么它们曾是 expecting 之后该 fiasco. Who hell leaks 该 sort 的 information? 我们是 losing millions 与
book_lore.resignation_note.page.1=这是 ME who的一 out 的 job now. 我是一正在 asked 至 resign. 我 hope 你 asshats finally learn 来自你的 overabundance 的 mistakes 与 take 该 stick out 的你的作为.
book_lore.resignation_note.page.2=我是不 coming 后上 Friday. Just send paycheck.

book_lore.memo_stocks.name=Intracorporate Memorandum
book_lore.memo_stocks.page.0=Investor Relations - $ $ 存在已经一些 glaring discrepancies 中 figures provided 用于 latest quarterly report. 它会为 prudent 用于 financial department 至制造一些 adjustments, 因此 there 不会为任何 concern.

book_lore.memo_schrab_gsa.name=Internal Memorandum
book_lore.memo_schrab_gsa.page.0=Contract Management - $ $ Legal has 制成 breakthrough 带 DLA. They已经 awarded us 带 45 BILLION GSA Schedule 用于 further procurement 与 research 的 saralloy. 在当前 estimates, 该会为在最小
book_lore.memo_schrab_gsa.page.1=40%% profit 上 related operations, let alone possibility 的 future contracts. 由于 confidential nature, 全部 fiscal evidence 是至 remain private.

book_lore.memo_schrab_rd.name=Internal Memorandum
book_lore.memo_schrab_rd.page.0=Research & Development - $ $ 我们的 main 生产 method 的 saralloy has 已经 through new 粒子加速器. However, 能量 costs 是 exorbitantly 高 compared 至数量的输出.
book_lore.memo_schrab_rd.page.1=Doctor Schrabauer, however, has discovered new interaction - called "Strange Lepton Oscillation" - 该 could significantly reduce costs. Through 不 entirely understood 处理, supplied 电子是 transmuted 进入 extremely
book_lore.memo_schrab_rd.page.2=high-energy 光子, through strange charm. 此是 extreme exception 至 many established 粒子 conversion laws, but preliminary experiments have proved 该这些质子 transmute 进入上与下 quarks, eventually creating saralloy.
book_lore.memo_schrab_rd.page.3=Strangely, 原型需要钨 alloyed 带小型数量的 saralloy. 中 addition, special 电容器为必需至 negate leftover positive 装药.

book_lore.memo_schrab_nuke.name=Research Report
book_lore.memo_schrab_nuke.author=Doctor Schrabauer
book_lore.memo_schrab_nuke.page.0=我们的多数 recent investigation led us 至 effects 的核 explosions 上材料. Thanks 至我们的 grant money, 我们 *accidentally* tested 我们的 theory 上 direct saralloy 合成来自铀.
book_lore.memo_schrab_nuke.page.1=仅我们的粒子加速器 has actually created saralloy previously. However, 在我们的 underground shot 在 Everwerpen, miniscule traces 的 saralloy 曾是 found 中铀矿石在 site. 全部 pure, metallic 铀 nearby had fissioned.
book_lore.memo_schrab_nuke.page.2=作为 such, given enough 铀矿石 concentrated around 炸药, 或 perhaps even 污染炸弹 rich 中废料含有 fissionable 材料, 一 could hypothetically 制造 enough saralloy 至 collect manually.

book_lore.bf_bomb_1.name=Private 不
book_lore.bf_bomb_1.author=M. Porter
book_lore.bf_bomb_1.page.0=Took 远程 enough, but my 传输曾是 accepted. 那些 new grads 曾是已经 hard 至 handle, let alone 全部 unprofessionalism 的铅. $ 不全部 good news - 此 lab 曾是 withholding further detail, 与我 did不需要更多 chaos over another magic new discovery.
book_lore.bf_bomb_1.page.1=的 course 该曾是 case. alumni had 它们的 doubts (surprising, considering 如何 bright-eyed 它们曾是), but my 仅... competent? colleague actually got 他的 hands 上 primer hand-out. 必须 have 更多 connections 比我 thought. 他的 memo 是 discouraging:
book_lore.bf_bomb_1.page.2=apparently, 存在 yet ANOTHER miracle 材料该它们 prodded out 的一些 concoction 的反物质与 fringe isotope. brochure calls 它 "SWIRLMAT" - hell 如果我 know - 与 that的它. 无 wonder 它们 wanted theoretical physicist,
book_lore.bf_bomb_1.page.3=它们不要 even know 什么它是 yet. Either way, practically 任何 job 会为 better 比 my 旧位置, 因此我无法 complain much about sketchiness.

book_lore.bf_bomb_2.name=Private 不
book_lore.bf_bomb_2.author=M. Porter
book_lore.bf_bomb_2.page.0=Despite absence 的 information 中该 primer, 我仍 had 一些 hope 它们 knew bit 更多. 不在全部. Every other senior researcher has blind faith 中此材料; 它们的 propositions 曾是 practically biblical. 我曾是 near speechless.
book_lore.bf_bomb_2.page.1=与 yet 我无法 even blame them. Swirlmat 制造无 goddamn sense - 它是 completely unlike 任何 other substance 我已经 seen 之前. 其 appearance 曾是 near frightening, literal mass 的 swirling colors, 带 darker lines permeating through neon 绿色 surface.
book_lore.bf_bomb_2.page.2=Even worse, 此 thing 是能量源. existence 的我们的 sample 是 violation 的 ALARA： lab 曾是 vacated 当它 arrived, 与仅 person brave enough (一 Dr. Melfyn) donned 等级 hazmat just 至 carry 它 20 meters.
book_lore.bf_bomb_2.page.3=empirical data is不 better, 作为我们是 breaking 第一 law 的 thermodynamics 带如何 much 能量它 radiates. 正在 anywhere near 该 thing - even behind meter 的铅 - 曾是 terrifying. 我们 sprinted out 的腔室 upon conclusion 的 spectroscopy
book_lore.bf_bomb_2.page.4=与我们 got nothing new out 的它. 那些 idiots 中 science team, god, did 不 even waver 之后全部该. Sitting through 那些 "discussions" 曾是 horrible; 该 quack 的头部 researcher even rumored 该 test ban 会为 lifted, 该我们 could 为
book_lore.bf_bomb_2.page.5=building 炸弹 out 的 shit 中 coming weeks, who 中它们的右 mind 会 work 上该? Hell, 一 sane assistant ( Andrew) nicknamed 它 "balefire" - 因为 burning 至 death 上 funeral pyre 会为 painless 由 comparison.

book_lore.bf_bomb_3.name=Private 不
book_lore.bf_bomb_3.author=M. Porter
book_lore.bf_bomb_3.page.0=team 与我 have 制成一些 breakthroughs. Emphasis 上分离 - isolating myself 来自更多 devout has 制成 working there 因此 much 更多 bearable. 同时我们仍 have 无 idea about actual properties 的 balefire (这是 difficult 至 analyze
book_lore.bf_bomb_3.page.1=sample 该 fries 你的 equipment) 其 interactions 带 other matter has proved fruitful. Notably, 它们 synthesized "气态" form：Andrew, 的全部 people, informed me 该它曾是 really colloid consisting 的 microscopic balefire 粒子, suspended 中一些
book_lore.bf_bomb_3.page.2=noble 气体. Each 粒子是 enveloped 由 positively-charged 'bubble' 的 ionized 气体, preventing 它来自 settling. Who could已经 guessed 该 fatal gamma 辐射 had benefit? 不 me. $ 我是 choosing 不至 think about 如何它们 transformed sample 进入
book_lore.bf_bomb_3.page.3=particulate, but 我无法 understate utility 的此气态 balefire - 这是制成它 much safer 至 experiment 上. $ Speaking 的 safety, 头部 researcher (中 act 的 callous disregard) 制成 discovery 该也 nearly took 他的头部 off.
book_lore.bf_bomb_3.page.4=他 decided 至 get "污染" 由 letting 单元的我们的 new colloid interact directly 带一些非常 expensive 反物质： resulting explosion turned 工作台它曾是上进入部件的 radiation-bleached slag, carved near-perfect hemisphere through
book_lore.bf_bomb_3.page.5=top, 与 gave 头部 healthy dose 的 ARS. 我 guess 我们 know 如何至制造它 explode now, but god, 一些 people...

book_lore.bf_bomb_4.name=Private 不
book_lore.bf_bomb_4.author=M. Porter
book_lore.bf_bomb_4.page.0=我 just 无法 escape my 旧 work. 它们是仅 place that的 hiring despite 全部此 godforsaken turmoil, but 我是不 going 后进入该 hole. $ 它们仅 tempted me 因为我需要 out, fast. Remember 该 atmospheric testing treaty 我们 withdrew 来自 week ago?
book_lore.bf_bomb_4.page.1=Well, dipshit 中装药的我们的 lab got something 右用于 once. denunciation came 带 flurry 的 new "scientists" joining, just 因此我们 could weaponize balefire. lack 的 critical thought here 是 honestly baffling - bless him, Andrew even jumped ship
book_lore.bf_bomb_4.page.2=第二第一 fucking 炸弹 DESIGN 曾是 drafted. 该作为 Melfyn looked 因此 happy 带他的 little 机构 - perhaps 他 got brainworms 来自 carrying 该 sample? - 其 involved 一些 stupid shit 使用 solidified, base balefire 与 HV
book_lore.bf_bomb_4.page.3=电池. $ Apparently, form matters 用于能量输出与 activation method 或无所谓, kind 的 like 铀 versus 钚中 regular nukes, but end result 是 initial shock starting explosion. 我 find 它 funny, hilarious even.
book_lore.bf_bomb_4.page.4=全部的 them place such emphasis 上 activation; 它们 ignore actual 机构的它全部因为它们不要 have single clue 如何它 works! 它可能作为 well 为 magic 在此 point, 与 yet 它们是仍 trying 至 twist 与 bend 它 - just 用于更多 weapons 的 war.

book_lore.bf_bomb_5.name=Private 不
book_lore.bf_bomb_5.author=M. Porter
book_lore.bf_bomb_5.page.0=我 just... 无法 come 至 grips 带它, even days 之后. 它曾是 foregone conclusion, really, 带如何 flippant science team 曾是带 safety. $ $ Doctor Melfyn, M.S., 是 gone. Dead, maybe. 我 saw 它 happen 之前 my own eyes, 中它们的 test 腔室.
book_lore.bf_bomb_5.page.1=我们 had just gotten another batch 的 pure balefire, 与他 had recovered electrical equipment 与能量源至 test 他的 proposal. 我不要 know 什么 caused 它 (曾是电力上? had 他 begun too soon?), but 它 seemingly progressed 中 agonizingly slow motion,
book_lore.bf_bomb_5.page.2=作为 green-tinted 轻型 consumed 工作台, 电池, 与 Dr. Melfyn standing 仅 meter away. Even 当工作台 had degraded 进入 pool 的 broiling 金属上地板, 他 did 不燃烧. 我不要 know 什么我 saw 中他的 eyes... $ $ Terror, 或 awe
book_lore.bf_bomb_5.page.3=over 他的 continued survival, maybe? 无所谓我们的 "miracle" 材料曾是, 它 did不 care. 带 bright blaze 的轻型, 他 disappeared 中下一个 moment. 曾是他 evaporated? incinerated? annihilated? sent 至 fucking hell itself, 我不要 know anymore!
book_lore.bf_bomb_5.page.4=头部 researcher sickens me. Said 我们 could 为更多 careful, keep trucking, 无所谓 other morale-improving filth 他 spewed. 该 dipshit 不会 ever figure out 该 playing 带火焰会 get 你 burned. $ 我 did不 bother
book_lore.bf_bomb_5.page.5=resigning, 我 just grabbed my shit 与 ran 用于 hills. 不 like 它 matters, anyway; considering lack 的 calls, 与 mushroom 云该 rose over my (now former) workplace, they已经 either blown everything 上或 entered full-on 军用 jurisdiction.
book_lore.bf_bomb_5.page.6=存在 vital distinction 至为制成 between dissection 与 VIVISECTION, 一其曾是 clearly lost 上 them. 它们可 dissect 金属或 atoms 作为 much 作为它们 like, but tearing 进入, vivisecting reality itself 是仅 going 至 end 中更多 Dr. Melfyns. Who knows!
book_lore.bf_bomb_5.page.7=government wants 至 put 此 shit 进入炸弹之后全部, maybe we会 see couple 更多 wars, couple 更多 million resigned 至 fate worse 比 death. 它们无法 hide 此 forever. $ $ 我不要 care. 不 anymore. Please, god, let me go 后
book_lore.bf_bomb_5.page.8=至 actual science. $ $ Goddamnit, Mae, get ahold 的 yourself...

book_lore.beacon.name=信号 Beacon Instruction 手册
book_lore.beacon.author=Flim Flam Industries
book_lore.beacon.page.0=Thank 你用于你的 purchase 的 Mk.2 Illuminated 信号 Beacon (rev. 1.3)! 此小型手册会 provide 近程 introduction 中 operation 的 beacon, 以及其 inner workings.
book_lore.beacon.page.1=Chapter 1：Architecture $ Each 单元是 composed 的四 main 部件：控制电路, lantern, fog horn 与外壳其 houses other 部件. 用于 detailed explanation 的 main 电路, please
book_lore.beacon.page.2=refer 至电路 diagram found 上内部的 maintenance lid 的外壳. lantern 是制成上的 polycarbonate case 含有 dual-color 250 Watt halogen bulb 带标准 200mm socket, 替代部件
book_lore.beacon.page.3=用于 bulb 可为 ordered 来自我们的 stores. 第三 party bulbs 不是推荐, 作为我们无法 ensure safe operation. case 是制成来自 specialized zinc-coated 不锈钢与是 resistant 至 weathering.
book_lore.beacon.page.4=Chapter 2：Lantern $ lantern的主级使用是 providing 轻型用于 ease 的 maintenance 中 harsh weather conditions 以及状态 indicator. 应 power-on self test (POST) fail, lantern 会
book_lore.beacon.page.5=轻型上红色, otherwise 它会轻型上绿色. 便笺该 colors 可 vary 取决于 replacement bulb.
book_lore.beacon.page.6=Chapter 3：Fog Horn $ fog horn 是主级 communication 设备的 beacon. beacon 是 designed 用于 peer-to-peer (P2P) communication 以及用于 message broadcasting.
book_lore.beacon.page.7=Chapter 4：Peer-to-Peer $ 用于 details 上 communication, refer 至 communications handbook. 近程 rundown 的 establishing P2P connection follows：第一, beacon has 至 give "START CONNECTION" 信号,
book_lore.beacon.page.8=正在 single 远程 tone. 全部可用 peers 应 respond 带 single 远程 tone 作为 well (order specified 由 proximity, 以及 communication guidelines outlined 中 handbook, section "Responding 至 Connection")
book_lore.beacon.page.9=Once desired peer has responded, give "ACCEPT CONNECTION" 信号, 正在二远程 tones, peer 会然后也 respond 带二远程 tones. 全部 communication afterwards has 至 happen 使用 pre-negotiated 信号, 多数 commonly
book_lore.beacon.page.10=使用 FAR-5M 标准. Communication 会 end immediately 如果无标准 has 已经 negotiated, serving 作为 "ping". 应 communication continue, connection 可为 ended 使用 another 远程 single tone "END CONNECTION".
book_lore.beacon.page.11=Chapter 5：Warranty $ [ 页 intentionally 左 blank ]

cannery.f1=[ 压力机 F1 用于 help ]

cannery.centrifuge=气体离心机
cannery.centrifuge.0=气体离心机可为 supplied 带流体使用 regular 流体管道.
cannery.centrifuge.1=多数配方 require multiple 离心机. intermediate products 无法 transported via 管道.
cannery.centrifuge.2=此 side acts 作为连接器其输出 intermediate product 进入 adjacent 离心机.
cannery.centrifuge.3=六氟化铀可为已处理带 just 二离心机, 此 however 会产生铀燃料与 Uranium-238.
cannery.centrifuge.4=Fully 处理它进入 Uranium-235 与 Uranium-238 需要 total 的四离心机.
cannery.centrifuge.5=一些配方也 require 离心机 overclocking 升级.

cannery.crucible=铸造厂
cannery.crucible.0=铸造厂用于 smelt 或, 锭或 other metallic 物品用于 alloying 与至 cast them 进入 different shapes.
cannery.crucible.1=它需要外部热量源 connected 至 bottom, like 燃烧室.
cannery.crucible.2=Once heated 上, crucible 可为使用中二 ways, 带或无配方模板.
cannery.crucible.3=铸造厂 has 二储存缓冲区用于材料:
cannery.crucible.4=缓冲区至左是用于 §a副产物§r, 全部材料 smelted 无配方模板会 land here.
cannery.crucible.5=如果配方是 installed, 材料该不要 match 配方也会为 stored here.
cannery.crucible.6=材料中此缓冲区不会 react 带 each other, 它们只能为输出来自绿色出口用于 casting.
cannery.crucible.7=缓冲区至右是用于 §c配方§r, 如果配方是 installed 与该 particular 材料是 relevant 至该配方, 它会 land here.
cannery.crucible.8=材料会 slowly combine 进入输出材料其是 automatically 输出来自红色出口.
cannery.crucible.9=便笺该仅此缓冲区 handles 配方. 如果模板是 installed retroactively, 材料中副产物缓冲区不会 combine, nor 传输至配方缓冲区.
cannery.crucible.10=出口会输出材料 automatically, 如果目标是 valid, 例如铸造厂通道或 mold.
cannery.crucible.11=作为带全部铸造厂方块, 铲可用于移除全部材料来自铸造厂.

cannery.fensu=FEnSU
cannery.fensu.0=FEnSU 是 capable 的 storing absurd 数量的能量, over 9EHE (that的 nine followed 由 18 zeros).
cannery.fensu.1=存在仅一能量连接器其可为 found 上 bottom.
cannery.fensu.2=此是也仅 place 其中 FEnSU 可 receive redstone 信号.

cannery.firebox=燃烧室
cannery.firebox.0=燃烧室燃烧 flammable 物品至 generate 热量.
cannery.firebox.1=它可燃烧任何 flammable 物品, although higher quality 燃料例如 coal, 焦炭与固体燃料燃烧 longer 与 hotter.
cannery.firebox.2=热量是 given off 由铜 contact 在 top 的燃烧室. 机器带 identical contact 上 bottom 可 receive 热量由正在 placed 上 top 的燃烧室.
cannery.firebox.3=如果热量 is不正在使用上与热量缓冲区 becomes 满, 燃烧室会 shut off 至 prevent wasting 的燃料.
cannery.firebox.4=一 such 机器是 stirling 发动机, 其会 turn 热量 directly 进入能量.

cannery.foundryChannel=铸造厂通道
cannery.foundryChannel.0=铸造厂通道是使用至运输熔融材料来自铸造厂或储罐进入 molds.
cannery.foundryChannel.1=通道可 receive 材料 either 由 pouring 来自 top - via 出口或 directly 来自铸造厂 - 或来自 side 来自 other 通道.
cannery.foundryChannel.2=当 transporting 材料, 通道会 prioritize 方块 like 出口与 shallow molds.
cannery.foundryChannel.3=当它无法 supply 出口或 mold, 材料会然后 flow 进入 neighboring 通道.
cannery.foundryChannel.4=Leftover 材料可为 removed 由使用铲.

cannery.silex=FEL & SILEX
cannery.silex.0=Free 电子激光 (FEL) 使用能量与激光晶体至制造 powerful 激光 beam.
cannery.silex.1=请小心, 作为激光会燃烧/melt through weaker 方块...
cannery.silex.2=...but 不 blast-proof 上.
cannery.silex.3=FEL 用于电力激光 Isotope 分离腔室 (SILEX). FEL 与 SILEX have 至为至少二方块 apart.
cannery.silex.4=激光 has 至 enter through 玻璃 openings 的 SILEX. Aiming 它 wrong could destroy 它.
cannery.silex.5=openings 上 sides 可用于连接流体管道至 SILEX.
cannery.silex.6=中 addition 至二连接器上 sides, 存在第三 hidden 连接器在 bottom 来自其物品可为 extracted.
cannery.silex.7=Each 配方需要 specific 激光类型. 使用 stronger 类型比所需会处理物品 faster.
cannery.silex.8=一 FEL 可 supply 上至 5 SILEX. Each SILEX 必须一块 apart 来自一 another.

cannery.stirling=Stirling 发动机
cannery.stirling.0=Stirling 发动机使用热量能量来自外部源至制造电力.
cannery.stirling.1=它需要 placed 上 top 的 heat-producing 机器, 例如燃烧室.
cannery.stirling.2=数量的热量它可 utilize however 是 limited, overspinning 可铅至 catastrophic malfunction.
cannery.stirling.3=upgraded version 可 take significantly 更多热量无 breaking.


cannery.willow=芥子 Willow
cannery.willow.0=芥子 willow 是工厂该允许镉金属至为 harvested.
cannery.willow.1=Willows 可为 placed 上泥土, grass 或 even dead/oily 泥土, but 它们 require 水至 grow.
cannery.willow.2=Willows 可为 fertilized 带 bone meal 或工业 fertilizer. 它们不要需要轻型至 grow.
cannery.willow.3=之后第二 stage 的 growth, 它们会需要 extra 块的 space above them 至 grow further.
cannery.willow.4=之后 fourth stage 的 growth, 它们 require dead 或 oily 泥土 below them.
cannery.willow.5=此可为 done either 由 manually planting willows 上 dead/oily 泥土, 或由 having hydraulic fracking 塔 nearby 其 continuously contaminates ground.
cannery.willow.6=之后 reaching final stage, willow 会移除 contamination 来自 ground, reverting dead/oily 泥土后进入 regular 泥土.
cannery.willow.7=Now willow的树叶可为 harvested. Breaking top 块会滴小型 willow 工厂, 3-6 树叶与 keep bottom 部件的工厂 intact.
cannery.willow.8=Soon 工厂会 start growing 再次, yielding 更多树叶如果泥土是 replaced 带 oily 泥土. 树叶可为已处理进入镉粉末使用 Leaching 反应堆.
cannery.willow.9=Harvesting willow 树叶可为 automated 使用自动 buzzsaw, 它会仅 break 工厂该是 ready 用于 harvest.

